From: RK3308BS M1SOC build <build@localhost>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH] drm/atomic-helper: restore pre-enable-before-CRTC modeset order for RK3308 RGB/DPI panel

Between kernel 6.18.0 and 6.18.49, commit c12df0f5ca41 ("Revert
\"drm/atomic-helper: Re-order bridge chain pre-enable and post-disable\"")
changed drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_enables() so that the CRTC is
enabled BEFORE the encoder/bridge pre_enable step:

    6.18.0 : bridge pre_enable -> crtc_enable -> bridge_enable   (works)
    6.18.49: crtc_enable -> bridge pre_enable -> bridge_enable   (hangs)

On this board the panel is attached as a DPI panel-bridge
(drm_panel_bridge_add_typed(..., DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DPI) in the RK3308
RGB driver), so the bridge pre_enable IS the panel power/reset-GPIO
prepare sequence. With the 6.18.49 order the RK3308 VOP (CRTC) is
enabled and begins scanning out to the RGB/DPI pins before the panel has
been powered and taken out of reset, which hard-hangs the SoC during the
first fbdev modeset commit (confirmed via drm.debug: freeze immediately
after "[drm:drm_mode_addfb2] [FB:40]", i.e. the CRTC-enable commit).

The upstream revert was made because the pre_enable-first order
regressed OTHER platforms (R-Car, MCDE, newer Rockchip VOP2); the agreed
long-term fix is per-driver sequencing. This kernel is built for a single
board (RK3308 VOP1 + fixed RGB/DPI panel), so restoring the
pre_enable-first order here is safe and matches the exact sequence that
worked on 6.18.0 (v64-v67). Only the call ordering in the two helper
call sites is changed; the exported helper functions themselves are
untouched.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c
index b06a5cba5295..038f666091b5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c
@@ -1370,9 +1370,9 @@ disable_outputs(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_atomic_state *state)
 {
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_encoder_bridge_disable(dev, state);
 
-	drm_atomic_helper_commit_encoder_bridge_post_disable(dev, state);
-
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_crtc_disable(dev, state);
+
+	drm_atomic_helper_commit_encoder_bridge_post_disable(dev, state);
 }
 
 /**
@@ -1758,10 +1758,10 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(drm_atomic_helper_commit_encoder_bridge_enable);
 void drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_enables(struct drm_device *dev,
 					      struct drm_atomic_state *state)
 {
-	drm_atomic_helper_commit_crtc_enable(dev, state);
-
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_encoder_bridge_pre_enable(dev, state);
 
+	drm_atomic_helper_commit_crtc_enable(dev, state);
+
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_encoder_bridge_enable(dev, state);
 
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_writebacks(dev, state);
-- 
2.43.0
